                <pb facs="0731" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/310: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Riddle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-01T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Department’s 51, September 30, 5 p.m. As special ambassadors are to be
                    received by President Irigoyen to whom letters of credence will be presented 2
                    or 3 days prior to date of inauguration the Argentine Government desires that
                    procedure be uniform in all cases and that letters be addressed to him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Riddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
